  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building CPF Ineza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CPF INEZA (Staffs and Cooperatives)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICCO will provide capacity building support to INEZA cooperative in the following areas: 

Organizational analysis of INEZA, with Microscore to establish current institutional situation, areas for improvement and next steps. 

Analysis of the current credit systems, especially for agricultural loans and assess potential for improvement.  

Anaysis of the current reporting and MIS system and suggest areas for improvement  

Training and coaching on portfolio management and risk management for staff 

Training and coaching on the agricultural credit process including the A-CAT for loan officers staff. 

Regular coaching and performance assessment</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rabobank foundation has been a longstanding partner of ICCO-Terrafina, currently a program of ICCO-cooperation, whereby ICCO-Terrafina provided capacity building support to rural based financial service providers and Rabobank foundation provides loans and investments to the financial service providers that are partnering with  ICCO Terrafina. The joint objective of both parties is to increase access to finance for the Rwandan smallholder farmers. The current proposal fits within this overall objective in Rwanda   

The offer of agriculture products for CPF INEZA is a must as a financial institution located in rural area and semi urban area. However, the major problem is that its staff is not trained in agriculture financing and skills in this area is key to understand the agriculture seasons in Rwanda, which crops can be financed?, what is the period of repayment for a specific crops?, where can we find the information needed for inputs and market? What are the risks related to the sector? etc. 

In addition to that, the institution does not have enough tools to ensure a proper assessment of    agriculture loan applications like the A- CAT tool, to minimize risks of delinquency related agriculture sector. INEZA&#x2019;s Agriculture products need to be reviewed and be tailored to needs of clients. They need also to be set into the MIS according to the features that will allow clients to repay their loans according to their cycles of production or period of harvest.  

In addition, CPF INEZA as well does not have a strategic plan which is a major document to guide the institution (Board, Management, and staff) to achieve vision, social mission, and strategic objectives.</narrative>
  </description>
